  "reason": "I audited the 92-concept inventory against the 13 existing hubs: every concept appears in exactly one group, every group is nonempty, and all titles are distinct, so the current partition is already a valid and complete cover. Reviewing it on the merits, the organization follows the corpus's two natural axes \u2014 biological subject matter (fitness landscapes, essentiality assays, pangenome evolution, ecotypes, metabolism and metabolic models, resistance/defense/mobile elements, subsurface ecology, translational applications) and methodological validity (sampling and confounding, annotation/dark-matter resolution, data infrastructure and provenance) \u2014 with the validity hubs kept adjacent to, but separate from, the biology they qualify. Borderline cases were checked individually and left in place: spatial-sampling-effort-confounding stays with Resistance, Defense Systems, and Mobile Elements because its confounded signal is specifically geographic resistance hotspots and it is only interpretable alongside the resistome claims; callability-limited-comparative-inference stays with Gene Essentiality and Perturbation-Assay Validity because callability is a property of perturbation collections; outer-membrane-lipid-homeostasis stays with Gene Fitness Landscapes and Cofitness Modules because its lipid A-loss rescue evidence is a fitness/cofitness result rather than a standalone envelope-biology topic; and lab-versus-nature concepts remain split from raw fitness architecture, since that hub argues about selection rather than about fitness measurement itself. Moving any of these would fragment an existing argument thread for no inferential gain, so I made no identity or membership changes \u2014 names and memberships are preserved exactly, which also keeps existing wikilinks and hub prose stable for the writer.",
  "version": 1
}
